# Publication workflow

Current expected state:

- Branch: `cur`
- Expected publication posture after sync: 8/8 main figures + 10/10 Extended Data
- Publication artifact stack: complete (ED1–ED10)
- Release/tag/archive/publish: approval-gated (not part of ED10 receipt execution)

Before work:

```bash
git fetch --all --prune
git switch cur
git pull --ff-only origin cur
git status --short
git rev-parse HEAD
python3 scripts/publication_inventory.py
```

Expected inventory:

```text
main figures: 8/8
extended data: 10/10
```

Release/archive (separate approval required):

- tag creation
- wheel/sdist build and publish
- GitHub release
- archive/DOI assignment

New publication artifacts follow this pattern:

- script: `scripts/publication/<name>.py`
- PNG: `figures/publication/<name>.png`
- manifest: `outputs/publication/<name>_manifest.json`
- optional receipt: `outputs/publication/<name>_receipt.json`

Validation:

```bash
python3 -m compileall -q scripts/publication jaxfne tests
python3 scripts/publication/<name>.py
python3 scripts/publication_inventory.py
python3 -m mkdocs build --strict
PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD=1 PYTHONPATH=. python3 -m pytest tests/test_api_smoke.py tests/test_root_import_lightweight.py -q --tb=line
```

Every publication manifest must preserve:

```text
physical_amplitude_claim_allowed: false
performance_claims_allowed: false
```

Use capability/evidence wording, not superiority wording.
